00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:39.560
Don Juan!

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.680
Now they'll pay you, now they'll pay you.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.340
But why am I not the last one?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.660
2,300, 420.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:51.380
Come on, don't play so much, we already have plenty of money left, change.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:52.840
Don't shut up.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:55.180
I thought the little money was much more important.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.780
And it is, ma'am. You're the only one who's winning.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.300
The others are losing.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:03.070
We're not going to play anymore, now it's going to be...

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.770
22 cents, 770.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.120
That's outrageous!

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.140
I've never seen him squeeze so often.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.000
It's like 3,000 pesos.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:18.740
Oh, Jesus, we're about to buy the pension house.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.180
With this and our savings.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.520
Don't play anymore, Candida. Let's go.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:25.080
I'm going to leave him now that he's learned to play.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.280
What's wrong with him, Mr. Juan?

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:29.690
I had a bad idea bringing them here, didn't I?

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:33.940
I've already lost everything I had.

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.360
Look what you're doing, you don't know.

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:40.330
Now you're going to go out on the 14th.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.320
Oh, I don't think so.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:43.480
He's going to play black.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:44.420
What's that?

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.660
Nothing, but I wouldn't play him.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:47.680
Oh, you're crazy.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:48.760
He's not going anymore.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.380
Huh? He's not going anymore, ma'am. He's not going anymore.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:52.360
He's not going anymore, ma'am.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.540
Come on, uncle, this one doesn't want to play.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:55.340
Black on the 26th.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.420
On the 26th, free.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.680
Heh, you see?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.060
Come on, what number?

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:05.560
The first one to go, don't complain.

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:06.340
You lost.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.140
Come on, man, these eyes are robbers.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.050
Grab these bones here.

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:13.480
But what are you doing?

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.440
Going north of Sa Giras.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.110
To me? Look at these eyes.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:18.210
But where are you going?

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:19.690
Ah, to Buenos Aires with the first train.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:20.280
Hey!

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:20.640
Hey!

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:23.520
Stop!

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:24.930
You're not going anywhere.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:28.430
Come home and grow a little more.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.280
Yes, are you afraid of going back to the roulette?

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.980
We are afraid of not arriving in time to Buenos Aires.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:39.230
Yes, because we are in deals to buy a house of goods.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:41.320
A pension, as we say here.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.880
That's it. And we didn't get the money, you know.

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:49.690
But now, with this little money from the game, well, from the robbery,

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.560
it's enough and we're still going to have something left.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.140
Yes, you have been lucky.

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.730
Don't forget to come and visit us when I come back, Don Juan, eh?

00:19:58.030 --> 00:19:59.950
And if you want to come and stay there...

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.330
Just think about it, we'll give you a special price.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:03.820
Thank you very much.

00:20:04.190 --> 00:20:08.430
But now, since I lost my memory and had to leave the theater,

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:12.570
I live at a friend's house that the poor man doesn't charge me anything.

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.670
Ah, well, you shouldn't be changing that price.

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:19.050
Of course, but you come to drink a cup from time to time.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:20.960
Thank you very much, but...

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:27.160
Who knows if I'll go back to Buenos Aires.

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:29.590
The four pesos I brought...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.120
They took them from there.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:32.160
Hello, Rolita.

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:33.260
Did you lose a lot?

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:36.220
I've played up to the return ticket, ma'am.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.300
I don't know what's going to happen to me.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:41.860
If you lose, what do you do, Don Juan?

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:43.690
Ma'am, you're offending me.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.770
A Spaniard doesn't accept money from a lady.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.090
Let's go. I have 20 pesos and I'll give it to Ramiro.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:51.550
No way, ma'am.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:54.580
Would you prefer to throw me on that train you're going to take now,

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:56.650
rather than tarnish my dignity,

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:58.280
such villain?

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:04.740
Now, if you want to give those nickels to your husband,

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.600
I won't have any problem in affecting your husband,

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:09.630
but I'll never do that to a lady.

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:13.110
Give me a candy. Take it, Mr. Juan.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:16.970
Thank you, thank you very much. You save my life.

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:19.270
What a delicacy, huh?

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:22.840
Spain and I are like that, sir.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:04.050
to make of all those who surround us a family,

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:07.800
where we are like tomatoes,

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.530
and where children, husbands and other children

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:18.860
feel affection, respect and consent for each and every one of us.

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:20.810
What does it say?

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:24.020
All for one and one for one,

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:26.170
only for the bread and for the man,

00:22:26.770 --> 00:22:29.890
and the one who does not take care of his spirit is only one.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:59.300
an animal, praying to the serpents, and said to be without personal illusions, with which I am going to demonstrate a theory, that if I, that although it is true that, come on, because, because, well, as Acarca says this, well, well, and so on,

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:09.840
And to begin with, langoustines with mayonnaise.

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:12.910
Brought especially from Mar del Plata by its owners.

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:15.410
But these langoustines are fresh.

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:17.850
Fresh? Are you going to give them to me?

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:19.510
But they are from today.

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:21.430
Yes sir, from today, eight days ago.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:24.880
No, bring me what follows.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.720
What follows this is an indigestion.

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:32.250
Well, I don't know, I just take it very delicately.

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:36.480
What's the matter, Rayo?

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:37.740
It's nothing serious, ma'am.

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:40.170
It's the little girl Pepita who is giving her singing lesson.

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:44.290
What does that look like, Jesús?

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:45.830
We have a bird in the house.

00:23:46.010 --> 00:23:46.640
I'm going to see.

00:26:00.732 --> 00:26:02.732
Oh

00:26:30.510 --> 00:26:34.140
Since mom left without a job, we could not pay.

00:26:34.960 --> 00:26:35.720
And where is your mom?

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:38.270
A week ago she went on tour with a company.

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:40.600
Oh, I'm the daughter of the artist!

00:26:41.520 --> 00:26:42.360
Yes, ma'am.

00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:44.520
And how did you leave her alone here?

00:26:44.780 --> 00:26:47.490
Because with what she earns, I could not take her.

00:26:48.030 --> 00:26:50.070
You must come to my pension, right?

00:26:50.270 --> 00:26:53.250
Yes, ma'am. But as soon as my mom returns from the tour, we will pay her.

00:26:53.630 --> 00:26:57.510
My mom wanted to leave me at my aunt's house.

00:26:57.550 --> 00:26:59.540
But I cry so much because she left me here.

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:01.420
Because my aunt knows.

00:27:02.340 --> 00:27:03.730
Yes, it will be an aunt.

00:27:04.110 --> 00:27:04.910
Don't leave me anymore.

00:27:05.980 --> 00:27:07.000
She doesn't love me.

00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:08.780
But you can't wait.

00:27:09.260 --> 00:27:11.410
Who tells you anything to make you cry?

00:27:12.370 --> 00:27:14.180
I don't want to make you cry, daughter.

00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:19.200
But who calls you so often?

00:27:19.680 --> 00:27:20.680
It's Miss Lidia, boss.

00:27:20.860 --> 00:27:22.340
But I can't attend to her and serve her the food.

00:27:22.620 --> 00:27:23.920
It's a joke, wait for her.

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:25.800
Or get up earlier, like us.

00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:27.980
Also, you have to see at what time she goes to bed.

00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:29.980
Yesterday she came at five o'clock.

00:27:30.840 --> 00:27:34.100
At 5 in the morning, he'll work quietly.

00:27:34.580 --> 00:27:36.640
Quietly? And I'll call him Italian.

00:27:37.120 --> 00:27:38.980
Oh, he's Italian.

00:27:39.840 --> 00:27:44.040
But you don't know Lili Adeliz, the radio star.

00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:45.540
No, no, I don't.

00:27:46.340 --> 00:27:52.050
She's going to waste her time.

00:27:52.130 --> 00:27:55.360
She suffers the most from those who listen to her on the radio.

00:27:55.540 --> 00:27:56.340
What do I do, boss?

00:27:57.200 --> 00:27:59.080
I'll go attend to her.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:00.780
What do you mean, what do you mean?

00:28:00.900 --> 00:28:02.360
I'm telling you to go to the last room.

00:28:02.540 --> 00:28:04.980
I've been kissing your mom, huh?

00:28:05.080 --> 00:28:06.180
She was a great artist.

00:28:06.540 --> 00:28:07.550
Was she poor?

00:28:08.040 --> 00:28:08.620
Well, well.

00:28:08.880 --> 00:28:11.940
You're going to stay here until your mom comes back.

00:28:12.140 --> 00:28:13.380
They'll sell you time for better.

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:15.000
Now, lunch.

00:28:15.460 --> 00:28:15.760
Let's go.

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:17.500
No, ma'am, we don't have lunch.

00:28:17.680 --> 00:28:18.500
We only have half a pension.

00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:21.660
When mom left us without work,

00:28:21.780 --> 00:28:23.060
we arranged with the other boss

00:28:23.060 --> 00:28:24.940
so that it would be cheaper for us.

00:28:25.780 --> 00:28:26.540
Poor thing.

00:28:27.080 --> 00:28:29.870
Well, from today, your lunch is all ours.

00:28:32.270 --> 00:28:33.920
You're very good.

00:28:34.240 --> 00:28:34.800
Come on, come on.

00:28:34.920 --> 00:28:36.600
Close your eyes and walk.

00:28:39.180 --> 00:28:39.620
Finally.

00:28:40.140 --> 00:28:40.520
Come on.

00:28:40.940 --> 00:28:43.480
I can.

00:28:43.720 --> 00:28:45.080
Who are you?

00:28:45.880 --> 00:28:46.400
I'm...

00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:48.450
I'm the new boss of the house.

00:28:48.900 --> 00:28:49.040
Ah.

00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:50.320
What a pleasure.

00:28:50.780 --> 00:28:51.770
But come in.

00:28:52.290 --> 00:28:52.610
Eh...

00:28:52.610 --> 00:28:53.450
The pleasure is mine.

00:28:53.900 --> 00:28:56.460
But you'll have to apologize that I made you wait.

00:28:57.200 --> 00:28:57.520
But...

00:28:57.520 --> 00:28:58.660
But it's...

00:28:58.660 --> 00:28:59.750
It's nothing.

00:28:59.910 --> 00:28:59.970
It's nothing.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.620
No, it's nothing. Can you open the balcony for me?

00:29:02.620 --> 00:29:02.960
Of course.

00:29:03.540 --> 00:29:07.700
Calculate, the mokama is serving the table, and my lady...

00:29:07.700 --> 00:29:09.500
I understand, I understand.

00:29:10.160 --> 00:29:15.430
Now, if you want something, I...

00:29:15.430 --> 00:29:17.970
Can you be so kind as to bring me a coffee with milk?

00:29:18.330 --> 00:29:20.310
With milk, and with a lot of sugar.

00:29:21.980 --> 00:29:23.180
How nice.

00:29:23.980 --> 00:29:26.130
Thank you very much, but you're too nice.

00:29:27.090 --> 00:29:28.850
You have such a sharp eye.

00:29:30.410 --> 00:29:30.970
I brought yours.

00:29:32.490 --> 00:29:34.480
Oh, I'm not worth anything like this.

00:29:34.500 --> 00:29:36.070
You'll see, I'm well-arranged.

00:29:36.450 --> 00:29:38.910
And I'm not worth anything like this either, you know.

00:29:39.540 --> 00:29:42.240
Do you want me to comb your hair?

00:29:42.400 --> 00:29:43.920
Yes, with pleasure and with great pleasure.

00:29:45.460 --> 00:29:53.730
It smells so good here, huh?

00:29:54.200 --> 00:29:54.920
It's not from Paris.

00:29:55.120 --> 00:29:55.790
It's my perfume.

00:29:56.130 --> 00:29:58.130
Do you want some? Come on.

00:30:00.440 --> 00:30:00.800
Come on.

00:30:04.920 --> 00:30:06.390
You're very ticklish.

00:30:06.850 --> 00:30:08.410
The one who has an order that...

00:30:08.410 --> 00:30:08.630
What?

00:30:10.330 --> 00:30:11.150
I'm going for the coffee.

00:30:11.950 --> 00:30:13.250
And when you get back to the bathroom,

00:30:13.510 --> 00:30:14.290
I'll tell you what else I want.

00:30:14.980 --> 00:30:16.640
If you want me to take you to the bathroom,

00:30:16.800 --> 00:30:18.600
for me, the house is fulfilled, you see.

00:30:58.000 --> 00:30:58.280
Captain!

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:00.900
Where is he coming from?

00:31:11.460 --> 00:31:12.820
Where is the butter?

00:31:13.180 --> 00:31:13.950
In the fridge.

00:31:19.460 --> 00:31:25.610
What are you doing there?

00:31:26.570 --> 00:31:27.470
Nothing, what do you want?

00:31:27.710 --> 00:31:29.740
Prepare the breakfast for the lady.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:35.020
Listen, Lidia, it was half an hour ago that I rang the bell without anyone taking care of it.

00:31:36.070 --> 00:31:37.290
Oh, Lidia...

00:31:37.290 --> 00:31:41.340
Of course, you're going to move somewhere, I don't know where, to La Mocama.

00:31:41.820 --> 00:31:44.340
And what about Lora Pacholí? What does she want here?

00:31:44.850 --> 00:31:46.090
It will be the Langostinos.

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.780
What are you talking about, Langostino? Bring her to me.

00:31:49.410 --> 00:31:51.370
There's still a woman who doesn't know you yet.

00:31:51.470 --> 00:31:53.040
But she's going to know me right away.

00:31:53.690 --> 00:31:57.030
But how are you going to get up, not less than the boss, to serve a pensioner?

00:31:57.330 --> 00:31:59.150
And you're going to be the boss.

00:31:59.350 --> 00:31:59.970
But I'm...

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.760
Hey, man, come on, let me cool down.

00:32:01.880 --> 00:32:03.420
Bring that tray, Jesús.

00:32:04.460 --> 00:32:05.280
Let's rest our feet.

00:32:06.920 --> 00:32:08.300
I'm already sweating a lot.

00:32:08.930 --> 00:32:10.350
They are the langoustines, woman.

00:32:10.770 --> 00:32:22.120
They have already sent me the lunch.

00:32:24.880 --> 00:32:25.940
Come on, dear friends.

00:32:34.190 --> 00:32:35.280
It's me, the boss.

00:32:35.760 --> 00:32:38.530
Ah, I thought it was your husband.

00:32:39.010 --> 00:32:41.130
You got it wrong, it's your wife.

00:32:41.650 --> 00:32:41.710
Ah.

00:32:42.810 --> 00:32:45.240
And you're going to receive my husband like this?

00:32:45.380 --> 00:32:47.450
Poor thing, he's so good.

00:32:48.260 --> 00:32:49.460
Your wife is good.

00:32:49.970 --> 00:32:50.610
What did you say?

00:32:50.790 --> 00:32:52.590
What did you say, mom? Where did you leave him for breakfast?

00:32:52.910 --> 00:32:53.370
On the table.

00:32:53.750 --> 00:32:54.940
Did you bring any pastas?

00:32:55.020 --> 00:32:56.420
No, I brought him fresh bread.

00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:58.360
Oh no, fresh bread makes you fat.

00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:03.780
Your sister likes to get fat a little, so as not to show off her muscles.

00:33:04.140 --> 00:33:06.960
At least that way she would have a reason for so many cuts.

00:33:07.380 --> 00:33:11.550
Get fat? God forbid! Men prefer silhouettes.

00:33:11.830 --> 00:33:15.910
What men prefer is shame, with silhouettes or without silhouettes.

00:33:17.480 --> 00:33:21.810
But from what I see in this house, what I prefer is morality, a lot of morality.

00:33:23.880 --> 00:33:25.660
If she doesn't like it, she looks for her comfort.

00:33:26.040 --> 00:33:29.520
I would do more.

00:33:35.180 --> 00:33:36.810
You'll see her tonight. Bye, Richard.

00:33:37.110 --> 00:33:37.630
You're leaving already?

00:33:37.930 --> 00:33:38.830
Yes, sir. I'm working.

00:33:39.170 --> 00:33:39.490
Employee?

00:33:39.630 --> 00:33:41.520
At the restaurant for you, yes, sir. Enjoy.

00:33:42.520 --> 00:33:43.160
Bye, precious.

00:33:43.820 --> 00:33:45.060
Don't you want me to accompany you?

00:33:45.500 --> 00:33:46.300
I'm not going to the university.

00:33:46.700 --> 00:33:47.780
I don't like students.

00:33:48.520 --> 00:33:52.020
I like painters.

00:33:52.910 --> 00:33:53.830
Well, forget it.

00:33:53.950 --> 00:33:54.070
What?

00:33:54.460 --> 00:33:55.960
Haven't I seen you, during the whole lunch,

00:33:56.200 --> 00:33:57.200
devouring yourself with your eyes?

00:33:57.400 --> 00:33:57.560
Me?

00:33:57.880 --> 00:33:59.040
You! Tell me! Are you going to tell me?

00:33:59.570 --> 00:33:59.890
I'm going to...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.420
She's very jealous.

00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:04.730
She's unbearable.

00:34:04.770 --> 00:34:06.070
She thinks all women die for her.

00:34:07.460 --> 00:34:09.360
Poor thing, with that face.

00:34:09.740 --> 00:34:10.440
What does she have on her face?

00:34:10.580 --> 00:34:10.860
She's pretty.

00:34:11.570 --> 00:34:12.730
That's why I've painted you a lot.

00:34:13.240 --> 00:34:14.020
That's calling me pretty.

00:34:14.320 --> 00:34:16.400
Oh no, I'll kill myself.

00:34:16.620 --> 00:34:22.310
Why is she so jealous?

00:34:22.410 --> 00:34:23.110
She's very jealous.

00:34:23.330 --> 00:34:24.310
She hates everything.

00:34:24.710 --> 00:34:25.610
She hates me.

00:34:26.850 --> 00:34:27.950
She hates him.

00:34:28.090 --> 00:34:28.590
Oh, as if.

00:34:41.580 --> 00:34:42.080
I'm going to kill myself!

00:34:42.300 --> 00:34:49.260
I didn't tell you!

00:35:02.010 --> 00:35:02.130
I'm sorry, sir.

00:35:02.510 --> 00:35:03.410
I'm sorry, sir.

00:35:03.550 --> 00:35:04.270
I've lost consciousness.

00:35:04.930 --> 00:35:05.930
It's nothing, don't worry.

00:35:06.270 --> 00:35:07.170
He'll be back soon.

00:35:07.350 --> 00:35:08.170
He'll be back soon?

00:35:08.270 --> 00:35:09.890
You're going to take him to the plaza,

00:35:09.890 --> 00:35:10.410
and he'll be back?

00:35:10.830 --> 00:35:17.700
Ah, the one with all the chairs.

00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:19.020
Who called you?

00:35:19.080 --> 00:35:20.520
The telephone, Mr. Miguel Angel.

00:35:20.740 --> 00:35:20.860
Who?

00:35:22.060 --> 00:35:22.940
A woman.

00:35:23.300 --> 00:35:25.760
A woman?

00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:27.240
A woman, I think.

00:35:27.480 --> 00:35:29.040
She's a phony, but she's a woman.

00:35:34.060 --> 00:35:36.300
Miguel Angel. This is Maria Luís.

00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:37.690
Miguel Angel.

00:35:38.010 --> 00:35:39.980
Yes, doctor. How are you, doctor?

00:35:40.560 --> 00:35:41.940
Ah, can't you speak?

00:35:42.410 --> 00:35:43.690
No. Yes, yes.

00:35:44.080 --> 00:35:44.560
Um...

00:35:44.560 --> 00:35:45.580
How do you say, doctor?

00:35:46.020 --> 00:35:47.840
Is your little wife close by?

00:35:48.040 --> 00:35:49.160
Yes, right here.

00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.550
Right here or in the academy.

00:35:50.830 --> 00:35:51.490
Later, at seven.

00:35:55.040 --> 00:35:55.520
Understood.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.310
In the ideal academy.

00:35:58.600 --> 00:35:58.880
Yes.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.080
I'm going to go with a friend who wants to serve you as a model.

00:36:02.280 --> 00:36:05.720
She has a very nice body. Don't lie to me.

00:36:05.720 --> 00:36:09.420
Why don't you tell your brother?

00:36:09.600 --> 00:36:11.660
He has cut it.

00:36:11.860 --> 00:36:13.250
I can't take it anymore.

00:36:13.390 --> 00:36:14.680
What? Doctor?

00:36:17.470 --> 00:36:18.270
Stay calm.

00:36:18.890 --> 00:36:20.170
Go upstairs. Who is this woman?

00:36:21.040 --> 00:36:21.980
Calm down, ma'am.

00:36:22.120 --> 00:36:22.990
Calm down.

00:36:23.370 --> 00:36:25.370
Then one kills a woman and they say she is a murderer.

00:36:25.650 --> 00:36:26.210
Go upstairs.

00:36:26.710 --> 00:36:27.810
But again.

00:36:28.640 --> 00:36:29.280
Come on, boss.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:43.320
I know, because if you don't do it, you'll be married for three months, huh?

00:36:43.460 --> 00:36:44.930
For Balanjaña, huh?

00:36:45.170 --> 00:36:51.660
Oh, my God!

00:36:51.660 --> 00:36:53.300
Do you see that he is hitting us?

00:37:28.030 --> 00:37:29.890
Tell me, ma'am, in the market, for me...

00:37:30.500 --> 00:37:32.540
Let him have a drink, Don Juan.

00:37:32.940 --> 00:37:35.320
Before I want to ask you a big favor.

00:37:35.520 --> 00:37:37.350
Are we alone?

00:37:37.750 --> 00:37:38.790
Speak with confidence.

00:37:39.270 --> 00:37:42.010
I have a car there marking 1.40.

00:37:42.470 --> 00:37:45.070
Could you send me to pay until it changes?

00:37:45.410 --> 00:37:46.850
I'll change you, Don Juan.

00:37:47.210 --> 00:37:50.490
No, if I say until it changes my situation, because ...

00:37:50.490 --> 00:37:51.470
Oh, you don't have it.

00:37:51.890 --> 00:37:52.730
Not even ten dollars.

00:37:53.440 --> 00:37:56.080
If I hadn't taken the tram, but you already know the custom.

00:37:56.380 --> 00:37:59.100
In the tram you get on and you pay it as soon as you get on.

00:37:59.120 --> 00:37:59.820
That's the window.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.480
Get out of the car.

00:38:00.500 --> 00:38:01.100
You're the one who's taking it.

00:38:01.460 --> 00:38:02.960
You're the one who's taking it, for God's sake.

00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:04.480
But you can pay it whenever you want.

00:38:04.640 --> 00:38:06.620
Well, I'm going to pay it before you stop marking it.

00:38:07.260 --> 00:38:07.660
Lucea!

00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:09.240
Yes, boss?

00:38:09.640 --> 00:38:11.560
I'm going to pay you a taxi and go to the door.

00:38:11.800 --> 00:38:12.880
Give me my luggage.

00:38:13.180 --> 00:38:14.170
So you can pay?

00:38:14.490 --> 00:38:15.370
Yes, countryman.

00:38:15.920 --> 00:38:20.300
I've had the misfortune of losing that old friend who gave me generous hospitality,

00:38:20.780 --> 00:38:22.750
and I'm in the cochinacayo.

00:38:23.090 --> 00:38:27.360
Either you keep me a few days in this noble house, countryman,

00:38:27.520 --> 00:38:29.920
or I'll have to put myself in front of the first bus.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:31.220
The only thing I want is to have a baby.

00:38:32.300 --> 00:38:36.070
There was no lack of love, Mr. Juan. This is your house.

00:38:36.540 --> 00:38:37.480
Where do I put this?

00:38:37.720 --> 00:38:38.770
What are you doing?

00:38:39.990 --> 00:38:40.430
My luggage.

00:38:42.240 --> 00:38:44.200
Take it to Mr. Juan Carlos' room.

00:38:44.220 --> 00:38:45.080
Oh, thank you.

00:38:45.240 --> 00:38:47.240
You save my life for the second time.

00:38:47.620 --> 00:38:49.320
Don't worry, Mr. Juan.

00:38:50.430 --> 00:38:52.870
It takes four days to get back to life.

00:38:54.640 --> 00:38:57.200
And you couldn't have arrived earlier, could you?

00:38:57.220 --> 00:38:57.440
Yes.

00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:58.970
Yes, today is Candida's birthday.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:04.470
Yes, and we're going to give a party for all the pensioners, with dance and everything.

00:39:04.880 --> 00:39:05.220
Cheers!

00:39:06.200 --> 00:39:06.560
Cheers!

00:39:08.610 --> 00:39:09.030
Cheers!

00:39:09.110 --> 00:39:09.630
Cheers!

00:39:09.630 --> 00:39:11.580
Cheers, ma'am.

00:39:11.620 --> 00:39:16.080
We have gathered here to give you the tribute that your generosity deserves.

00:39:16.480 --> 00:39:22.110
And see, ma'am, in each of these cups, alfabas, alfabos, in honor of you.

00:39:23.570 --> 00:39:25.830
For the most sympathetic of the patrons.

00:39:26.070 --> 00:39:27.030
For the most sympathetic!

00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:33.190
I'd rather not want any more after my mother.

00:39:33.760 --> 00:39:39.270
Please, don't say that, you'll still make me cry for a thousand times.

00:39:39.810 --> 00:39:40.990
Come on, come on, come on!

00:39:43.810 --> 00:39:45.190
Come here, Carmen!

00:40:00.190 --> 00:40:09.290
You want peace, don't you?

00:40:09.650 --> 00:40:11.030
Yes, I do.

00:40:11.190 --> 00:40:14.460
It's enough to know that for me there is no other woman more than you.

00:40:15.170 --> 00:40:17.770
However, from time to time, you go out a lot at night.

00:40:18.210 --> 00:40:19.350
And for the friends, woman.

00:40:19.790 --> 00:40:21.580
If not, they call you a snob.

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:23.490
And last night you came drunk.

00:40:24.510 --> 00:40:25.810
And you drank with all your teeth.

00:40:26.030 --> 00:40:27.560
What do I lie? You came drunk.

00:40:27.920 --> 00:40:29.030
You didn't tell me yourself.

00:40:29.390 --> 00:40:29.970
And that except one...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.120
Look at what she says when she's drunk!

00:40:31.620 --> 00:40:34.280
You make me feel very nervous.

00:40:34.640 --> 00:40:36.000
I can't see who my husband is dancing with.

00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:41.460
He's dancing with the little girl.

00:40:41.740 --> 00:40:43.240
Poor him, if he dances with another woman.

00:40:43.360 --> 00:40:45.920
Don't you like that your husband dances with another woman?

00:40:46.200 --> 00:40:48.570
You wouldn't like to see me dancing with a man either.

00:40:48.630 --> 00:40:50.550
Ma'am, I think I'm very manly.

00:40:50.780 --> 00:40:51.000
Really?

00:40:52.200 --> 00:40:53.160
What do you mean, my age?

00:40:53.620 --> 00:40:58.250
Here where you see me, it hasn't been long since a woman killed herself for me in a car.

00:40:58.750 --> 00:40:59.510
Poor thing.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:00.660
Are you going to break your hands?

00:41:00.660 --> 00:41:01.140
Ma'am!

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:03.460
I'm despised and soaked in tears

00:42:03.460 --> 00:42:24.590
I don't have a handkerchief in front of me

00:42:24.590 --> 00:42:25.900
I steal it for the baby

00:42:32.780 --> 00:42:38.240
A handkerchief, a heart, with the lost handkerchief,

00:42:38.940 --> 00:42:49.450
from that handkerchief came the cruel day, with the...

00:42:58.690 --> 00:42:59.930
How many times...

00:43:00.730 --> 00:43:16.870
Now that my love is in pain, I carry one that gives me forgiveness.

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:42.440
It has more impetus than ever in life.

00:44:01.050 --> 00:44:03.710
Oh, how beautiful!

00:44:05.970 --> 00:44:07.950
Give me my present, dear.

00:44:08.290 --> 00:44:10.310
You'll forgive me if I couldn't come earlier,

00:44:10.350 --> 00:44:12.750
but I went up to eat with the radio director, you know?

00:44:13.070 --> 00:44:13.850
What are you talking about?

00:44:14.300 --> 00:44:15.520
Let's have a drink.

00:44:15.800 --> 00:44:20.740
With these flowers in the jar.

00:44:21.830 --> 00:44:24.520
What do you think of Don Juan?

00:44:25.220 --> 00:44:26.680
Mother, what a woman!

00:44:27.020 --> 00:44:29.280
And if you knew...

00:44:31.120 --> 00:44:31.300
See?

00:44:32.490 --> 00:44:32.810
What?

00:44:32.990 --> 00:44:35.190
That I fell in love with Gracia.

00:44:35.250 --> 00:44:35.550
What?

00:44:36.280 --> 00:44:37.690
Yes, me, Don Juan, me.

00:44:38.310 --> 00:44:39.310
I'll tell you.

00:44:39.670 --> 00:44:41.710
Be careful, fellow countryman.

00:44:41.970 --> 00:44:43.210
Look at you, what a woman.

00:44:43.570 --> 00:44:45.610
You look like a woman for...

00:44:45.610 --> 00:44:48.990
Don't you dare to say anything in front of Cándida, Don Juan.

00:44:49.210 --> 00:44:50.590
That he already has her in his eyes.

00:44:50.900 --> 00:44:52.080
He wants to throw her away and everything.

00:44:52.540 --> 00:44:54.480
When she's the best pensioner in the house.

00:44:54.720 --> 00:44:55.600
The one who pays more.

00:44:55.860 --> 00:44:57.380
And the only one who pays on time.

00:44:58.900 --> 00:44:59.340
Well...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:00.560
What do I do?

00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:04.780
Ah, come on, now I understand everything.

00:47:33.130 --> 00:47:33.950
Good morning, ma'am.

00:47:33.950 --> 00:47:34.430
Good morning.

00:47:34.550 --> 00:47:35.690
There's a piece here.

00:47:35.730 --> 00:47:37.360
Yes, sir. Do you want to see it?

00:47:37.480 --> 00:47:38.080
How much will it cost?

00:47:38.650 --> 00:47:39.350
110 pesos.

00:47:39.710 --> 00:47:40.030
Is there heating?

00:47:40.710 --> 00:47:41.330
No, not that.

00:47:41.710 --> 00:47:42.610
And hot water?

00:47:42.790 --> 00:47:44.770
First and third Saturday of each month.

00:47:44.870 --> 00:47:45.450
So there's no heating?

00:47:46.010 --> 00:47:47.210
No, sir. We don't have heating.

00:47:48.050 --> 00:47:50.190
But instead, you'll find sincerity.

00:47:51.260 --> 00:47:52.540
A lot of sincerity.

00:47:52.940 --> 00:47:55.160
Yes, but the price. I can't pay more than 20.

00:47:55.500 --> 00:47:58.020
Oh, not that. It's 110. Not a penny less.

00:47:58.330 --> 00:47:59.790
Now, if you want to pay more...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:05.760
Look, I can offer you that, by telling you that from the other pension, when I left, the boss was crying.

00:48:06.120 --> 00:48:09.210
Ah, well, it's not going to happen to me because I'm in a hurry.

00:48:09.990 --> 00:48:11.140
Well, I'll think about it.

00:48:11.430 --> 00:48:12.410
Well, go with God.

00:48:12.670 --> 00:48:16.510
Hey, Augusto, please, come back.

00:48:16.970 --> 00:48:19.180
The boss has arrived at the market with a lot of meat.

00:48:19.500 --> 00:48:20.320
Yes, ma'am.

00:48:20.320 --> 00:48:21.440
Thank you.

00:48:30.670 --> 00:48:30.850
Yes!

00:48:30.850 --> 00:48:58.280
Are you sure, boss?

00:48:59.320 --> 00:48:59.840
This is my friend!

00:49:00.280 --> 00:49:00.760
What a shame!

00:49:30.480 --> 00:49:33.360
A rich man from Lima!

00:49:35.480 --> 00:49:35.840
Shameless!

00:49:36.180 --> 00:49:37.700
Oh, but give me the money!

00:49:38.140 --> 00:49:39.320
Where did you leave it to be condemned?

00:49:39.620 --> 00:49:40.100
What are you going to do, boss?

00:49:40.690 --> 00:49:42.350
Wherever I find it, I'll kill him!

00:49:42.390 --> 00:49:44.140
And then I'll divorce him!

00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:47.320
Boss, don't do that!

00:49:47.380 --> 00:49:48.880
Maybe the poor man doesn't have the guilt!

00:49:49.020 --> 00:49:49.440
Of course not!

00:49:49.820 --> 00:49:50.140
Of course!

00:49:50.320 --> 00:49:51.460
You have to kill her!

00:49:51.520 --> 00:49:52.200
She's a witch!

00:49:52.720 --> 00:49:54.400
Maybe the boss has done some witchcraft to her!

00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:57.620
Well, you'll put her in the streets right now!

00:49:57.620 --> 00:49:58.080
Do it!

00:49:58.270 --> 00:49:58.630
No, boss!

00:49:58.970 --> 00:49:59.980
These witches are...

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:03.420
It was very dangerous. They killed two men for her. I don't know what to do with her.

00:50:03.420 --> 00:50:05.740
How can I not give her a body? It's the only thing she has.

00:50:05.960 --> 00:50:08.790
If you tell her, maybe she'll escape with the boss.

00:50:10.070 --> 00:50:12.720
That's right! Wait!

00:50:13.200 --> 00:50:16.310
I could do what the other boss I had did.

00:50:16.810 --> 00:50:19.620
Her husband also cursed her. One of these vampires, you know.

00:50:19.820 --> 00:50:20.470
What is this?

00:50:20.870 --> 00:50:23.570
She's going to consult a very wise goddess that is here.

00:50:23.790 --> 00:50:25.390
And in a few days...

00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:32.690
Goodbye, sister. And don't forget what I told you.

00:50:32.770 --> 00:50:33.530
No, no, mother.

00:50:33.850 --> 00:50:36.120
What's the first thing that comes to your mind?

00:50:36.160 --> 00:50:36.480
Mother.

00:50:43.980 --> 00:50:46.340
Mother Rosa Paredes. What a lady.

00:50:46.790 --> 00:50:48.510
She's so miraculous, as they told me.

00:50:48.830 --> 00:50:50.230
Holy hand, my dear.

00:50:50.500 --> 00:50:53.100
My husband was cured of an ulcer in the stomach,

00:50:53.320 --> 00:50:55.440
nothing more than with water and salt.

00:50:55.820 --> 00:50:57.020
Only with water and salt?

00:50:57.160 --> 00:50:59.380
Well, he's a doctor I know.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:02.540
He took my husband a weapon that he had in his body,

00:51:03.120 --> 00:51:04.540
Namaste, pumajo and gavón.

00:51:04.760 --> 00:51:08.080
Yes, but the doctors, for one that hits him in the back of the head,

00:51:08.420 --> 00:51:11.080
instead of the pink mother, if the sick man does not die in the past,

00:51:11.360 --> 00:51:12.320
they save him.

00:51:12.540 --> 00:51:15.740
And they say that after the organ, the passionate questions, the revenge.

00:51:16.720 --> 00:51:18.800
Ah, holy hands, holy hands.

00:51:19.140 --> 00:51:21.820
And that one divines all of them, and the servants ventilate them.

00:51:22.040 --> 00:51:24.650
But what kind of professor of hidden sciences did they receive here?

00:51:25.010 --> 00:51:27.730
From the pharaohs, they told me, because she divines diplomacy.

00:51:34.410 --> 00:51:51.890
The first one is from my sister.

00:51:51.990 --> 00:51:55.110
I was coming so you could give me the letters.

00:51:55.330 --> 00:51:56.510
Don't tell me anything, sister.

00:51:56.690 --> 00:51:58.010
I already did what you told me to do.

00:52:03.610 --> 00:52:04.610
Do you want to cut with your left hand?

00:52:04.770 --> 00:52:25.520
A woman who wants to break up your marriage.

00:52:26.540 --> 00:52:26.940
Cabal!

00:52:31.120 --> 00:52:31.740
She's an artist.

00:52:32.240 --> 00:52:34.480
She's a shameless woman, a bad-ass!

00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:36.060
Where are you?

00:52:36.200 --> 00:52:36.900
Is this her?

00:52:37.000 --> 00:52:37.900
Calm down, sister.

00:52:40.820 --> 00:52:41.340
Arzona!

00:52:43.430 --> 00:52:44.490
Here's another woman.

00:52:44.750 --> 00:52:46.660
But I've already married a dancer!

00:52:46.920 --> 00:52:50.060
This woman is a foreigner.

00:52:50.480 --> 00:52:51.660
But don't be afraid.

00:52:52.020 --> 00:52:53.630
This foreigner woman is you.

00:52:54.030 --> 00:52:56.030
It's me?

00:52:56.370 --> 00:52:58.520
You don't look like anything.

00:52:58.860 --> 00:52:59.970
And how did you...

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:01.360
You don't know that I'm a bloodsucker.

00:53:01.620 --> 00:53:03.160
That's what the letters say.

00:53:03.160 --> 00:53:05.970
Now I see blood.

00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:07.160
You're hurt.

00:53:07.600 --> 00:53:10.130
The letters say that there will be blood in your life.

00:53:10.350 --> 00:53:11.510
Or maybe there will be portions.

00:53:11.670 --> 00:53:12.770
I'll cut their heads off.

00:53:12.910 --> 00:53:14.790
No, that's how blood is cut off.

00:53:15.230 --> 00:53:15.910
Let her run.

00:53:16.560 --> 00:53:17.580
Don't stop drinking.

00:53:17.820 --> 00:53:18.600
Let her run.

00:53:19.520 --> 00:53:21.100
Here comes the artist again.

00:53:21.510 --> 00:53:23.330
My husband's reprimand gives him a hint.

00:53:30.730 --> 00:53:32.390
There's a man here who follows her.

00:53:32.630 --> 00:53:33.010
Where?

00:53:33.190 --> 00:53:33.600
On the horse.

00:53:34.000 --> 00:53:34.600
My husband.

00:53:34.940 --> 00:53:36.060
A grumpy man.

00:53:36.260 --> 00:53:36.740
Cascaño.

00:53:36.960 --> 00:53:38.960
Well, grumpy throwing rubies.

00:53:39.140 --> 00:53:39.700
That's it.

00:53:39.980 --> 00:53:41.000
My husband, well said.

00:53:41.460 --> 00:53:41.920
Enough!

00:53:42.470 --> 00:53:44.430
And what could I do to tie him up with me?

00:53:45.030 --> 00:53:46.430
Have confidence and faith.

00:53:46.730 --> 00:53:49.470
Listen to my advice and follow my instructions.

00:53:50.010 --> 00:53:50.550
And nothing else?

00:53:50.840 --> 00:53:52.400
And pay me what I like for my service.

00:53:52.720 --> 00:53:53.300
Whatever you want.

00:53:53.420 --> 00:53:54.430
Because I don't charge.

00:53:55.180 --> 00:53:58.830
God has put me in the world to do good and nothing else.

00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:02.450
Well, that's not good.

00:54:02.830 --> 00:54:03.930
What do you want, sister?

00:54:04.230 --> 00:54:05.170
I don't charge.

00:54:05.450 --> 00:54:09.340
They tell me four, five, whatever the customer wants.

00:54:09.540 --> 00:54:10.720
Three, then.

00:54:11.060 --> 00:54:13.910
Because, well looked after, it's better to take bad news.

00:54:14.250 --> 00:54:19.340
Sister, now the recipe for a party.

00:54:19.680 --> 00:54:21.080
What recipe?

00:54:21.710 --> 00:54:24.070
